{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'PR_0000(03264|03328|03353)|MCAM|MUC18|MYLK|collagen alpha-1\\\\(I\\\\) chain|collagen alpha-1\\\\(III\\\\) chain|myosin light chain kinase|cell surface glycoprotein MUC18' src/ontology/cl-edit.owl\"","aggregated_output":"3371:Declaration(Class(obo:PR_000003264))\n3372:Declaration(Class(obo:PR_000003328))\n3373:Declaration(Class(obo:PR_000003353))\n25537:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31857493\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35069694\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020013 \"A fibroblast forming the connective tissue sheath that encloses the hair follicle epithelium from the level of the bulge downward to the hair bulb. This cell expresses characteristic markers, including DPEP1 in humans and COL11A1 and ACTA2 (alpha-smooth muscle actin) in mice and humans. Dermal sheath fibroblast possesses contractile properties mediated by calcium-calmodulin-myosin light chain kinase signalling, generating centripetal force during hair follicle catagen that relocates the dermal papilla to the stem cell niche.\")\n25609:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020018 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003264))\n34302:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27199166\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34727990\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4052026 \"In humans, type IIx fiber contains high levels of MYLK2, enhancing contraction speed and force via myosin phosphorylation, especially under low calcium. This mechanism supports post-activation potentiation, increasing force output in fast-twitch muscles. Additionally, this fiber has abundant ACTN3 (α-actinin-3), linked to muscle power, and exhibits the highest shortening velocity among human muscle fiber types. Notably, type IIx fiber is selectively lost in aging-related sarcopenia, increases in proportion in type 2 diabetes and obesity, and is the first to degenerate in Duchenne Muscular Dystrophy, impacting muscle function across various conditions.\")\n35333:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072104 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003264))\n35334:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072104 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003328))\n35335:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072104 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003353))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
